me>Magnusson</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Milsom</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A population based study of Swedish women's opinions about antenatal, delivery and postpartum care</article-title><source>Acta Obstet Gynecol Scand</source><year>2001</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>130</fpage><lpage>36</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11167207</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1034/j.1600-0412.2001.080002130.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Olin</surname><given-names>R-M</given-names></name><name><surname>Faxelid</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Parents'need to talk about their experiences of childbirth</article-title><source>Scand J Caring Sci</source><year>2003</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>153</fpage><lpage>59</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12753516</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1471-6712.2003.00105.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Small</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Lumley</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Donohue</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Potter</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Waldenstr&#x000f6;m</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Randomised controlled trial of midwife led debriefing to reduce maternal depression after operative childbirth</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>2000</year><volume>321</volume><fpage>1043</fpage><lpage>47</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11053173</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmj.321.7268.1043</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Krippendorff</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><source>Content Analysis &#x02013; An Introduction to Its Methodology</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>Thousand Oaks, California: Sage publications</publisher-name><fpage>18</fpage><lpage>44</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Waldenstr&#x000f6;m</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Rudman</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hildingsson</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intrapartum and postpartum care in Sweden: women's opinion and risk for not being satisfied</article-title><source>Acta Obstet Gynecol Scand</source><year>2006</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>551</fpage><lpage>560</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16752233</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gibbins</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomson</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Women's expectations and experiences of childbirth</article-title><source>Midwifery</source><year>2001</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>302</fpage><lpage>13</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11749063</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1054/midw.2001.0263</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>B&#x000f6;rjesson</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Paperin</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindell</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Issues and innovations in nursing practice &#x02013; Maternal support during the first year of infancy</article-title><source>J Adv Nurs</source><year>2004</year><volume>45</volume><fpage>588</fpage><lpage>94</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15012636</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2648.2003.02950.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Alexander</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Confusing debriefing and defusing postnatally: the need for clarity of terms, purpose and value</article-title><source>Midwifery</source><year>1998</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>122</fpage><lpage>24</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10382482</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0266-6138(98)90010-9</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Axe</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Women's issues. Labour debriefing is crucial for good psychological care</article-title><source>British Journal of Midwifery</source><year>2000</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>626</fpage><lpage>28</lpage><comment>630-31.</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Charles</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Curtis</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Birth afterthoughts: a listening and information service</article-title><source>British Journal of Midwifery</source><year>1994</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>331</fpage><lpage>34</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Inglis</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Accessing a debriefing service following birth</article-title><source>British Journal of Midwifery</source><year>2002</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>370</fpage><lpage>71</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Antonovsky</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><source>Unraveling the mystery of health. How people manage stress and stay well</source><year>1987</year><publisher-name>San Fransisco, CA: Jossey-Bass</publisher-name><fpage>15</fpage><lpage>32</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Affonso</surname><given-names>DD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Missing pieces. A study of postpartum feelings</article-title><source>Birth Fam J</source><year>1977</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>159</fpage><lpage>64</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1523-536X.1977.tb01234.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rogan</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Shmied</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Barclay</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Everitt</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Wyllie</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Becoming a mother &#x02013; developing a new theory of early motherhood</article-title><source>J Adv Nurs</source><year>1997</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>877</fpage><lpage>85</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9147193</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2648.1997.1997025877.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Saisto</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ylikorkala</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Halmesm&#x000e4;ki</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Factors associated with fear of delivery in second pregnancies</article-title><source>Obstetrics and Gynecology</source><year>1999</year><volume>94</volume><fpage>679</fpage><lpage>82</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10546709</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0029-7844(99)00413-5</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>